{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD_ne_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD_ne_self","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L184-L190","doc":"**`z_D = q` forces `q = 0`.**  Convention D never reaches the first root of\n`y_(2,1)`, over ANY field — this one needs no ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_eq_neg_inv_qsq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_eq_neg_inv_qsq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L175-L182","doc":"**The other convention-C degeneracy `z_C = −1/q` is the corpus `detFactor4`.**\nIts only real root is `u = −ψ`, outside the `u > 0` regime — which is why the\ncorpus sees just one positive-`u` threshold despite two roots of `y_(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_eq_qsq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_eq_qsq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L161-L173","doc":"**The convention-C degeneracy `z_C = q` is the corpus `detFactor3`.**\nWith `q = u²` and `z_C(u) = u/(u²+1)`, the condition `z_C = q` is `u(u³+u−1) = 0`,\nwhose only nonzero root is the corpus threshold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L152-L159","doc":"**`z_D = 1` iff `q³ = q²+1`** — the supergolden equation.  This is a\nDIFFERENT point from the convention-C Gram degeneracy `u³+u−1 = 0` (there\n`u = √q`, so `q = 1/ψ²`); here it is `q = ψ` itself.  It is where the Markov\ntrace collapses onto the Frobenius counit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y3_at_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y3_at_zD","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L141-L150","doc":"**The trivial block at the canonical loop value.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21_at_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21_at_zD","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L129-L139","doc":"**The `(2,1)` weight at the canonical loop value is `q²/(q²+1)²`.**\nThe `(q²−q+1)(q²+q+1) = q⁴+q²+1` of the denominator cancels against the\nnumerator; nothing of the block structure survives except a square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y111_at_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y111_at_zD","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L117-L127","doc":"**`y_(1^3)` vanishes identically at the canonical loop value.**  This is the\nsame fact as `gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero`: convention D annihilates the sign block,\nwhich is why the D determinant is identically singular and cannot be used to\nlocate a transition — the question has to be put to the block weight instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L93-L115","doc":"**The `(2,1)` block degenerates at exactly two loop values.**\n`y_(2,1)(z) = 0` iff `z = q` or `z = -1/q`.  Both roots are needed below: under\nconvention C they are the corpus `detFactor3` and `detFactor4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.weights_sum_to_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.weights_sum_to_one","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L80-L91","doc":"**Markov normalisation.**  `y_(3) + 2 y_(2,1) + y_(1^3) = 1` for EVERY `z` —\nthe weights are a partition of the trace, not three independent quantities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L77-L78","doc":"The convention-C Markov parameter in the square-root variable `u`, `q = u^2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L74-L75","doc":"The canonical (convention-D) Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y111","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L70-L72","doc":"Wedderburn weight of the sign block `(1^3)`, with `z` free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L66-L68","doc":"Wedderburn weight of the two-dimensional block `(2,1)`, with `z` free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y3","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.lean#L62-L64","doc":"Wedderburn weight of the trivial block `(3)`, with the Markov loop `z` free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}